WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.598 --> 00:00:22.121
stared in horror as the energy flowed toward a wormhole blinking in the corner.

2
00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:27.285
Through the opening he caught a glimpse of the rough bark of the ancient Wormwood tree.

3
00:00:27.965 --> 00:00:31.027
It was too late—Magica was about to be destroyed!

4
00:00:31.828 --> 00:00:34.001
Suddenly Zann had an idea.

5
00:00:34.561 --> 00:00:35.442
He turned to the queen.

6
00:00:35.822 --> 00:00:38.644
"Your Majesty, summon all the wormholes!"

7
00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.186
For a second the Roodian queen looked confused.

8
00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:44.628
Then her eyes widened.

9
00:00:45.048 --> 00:00:47.950
She raised a hand, and the air buzzed with new energy.

10
00:00:48.911 --> 00:00:50.272
"What are you doing?"

11
00:00:50.612 --> 00:00:53.634
Morb snarled, still weakened from the mice's feeding.

12
00:00:54.474 --> 00:00:57.657
Suddenly the room was flooded with thousands of wormholes!

13
00:00:58.497 --> 00:00:59.558
Morb looked stunned.

14
00:00:59.578 --> 00:01:02.600
"What—how—" he stammered.

15
00:01:03.688 --> 00:01:07.749
Zann held his breath, hoping he was right about what would happen next.

16
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:14.831
If he was wrong, he might have just destroyed not only Magica, but also every other world.

17
00:01:15.552 --> 00:01:17.412
He glanced through a nearby wormhole.

18
00:01:18.112 --> 00:01:22.414
In a world he didn't recognize, a funny-looking dragon was nibbling on a tree.

19
00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:29.356
Bzzt! A tiny spurt of energy snaked in and fizzled out against the dragon's scaly side.

20
00:01:30.504 --> 00:01:35.026
Zann spun around and spotted the rough seas of Skellia through another wormhole.

21
00:01:35.626 --> 00:01:41.649
Bzzt! A gulper leaped up and swallowed a small blob of energy hovering over the waves.

22
00:01:42.429 --> 00:01:47.831
Everywhere he looked, Zann saw bits of energy fizzling out harmlessly in various worlds.

23
00:01:47.851 --> 00:01:49.572
"It worked!"

24
00:01:49.812 --> 00:01:50.252
he cried.

25
00:01:50.272 --> 00:01:55.574
"The energy got divided into so many different worlds that it became completely harmless!"

26
00:01:56.355 --> 00:01:58.276
"But how did you know that would happen?"

27
00:01:58.396 --> 00:01:59.016
Perda asked.

28
00:01:59.804 --> 00:02:00.545
Zann shrugged.

29
00:02:00.565 --> 00:02:07.930
"It was what Morb said about how something that's powerful in large amounts is harmless in small amounts."

30
00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.391
Morb gnashed his teeth.

31
00:02:09.811 --> 00:02:12.953
"I should have killed you when I had the chance!"

32
00:02:12.973 --> 00:02:15.015
"But you didn't."

33
00:02:15.695 --> 00:02:17.977
Wyssa stepped forward and snapped her fingers.

34
00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:20.659
Instantly Morb was shackled to her.

35
00:02:21.539 --> 00:02:24.802
Then she pointed at the contraption and muttered a few words.

36
00:02:25.582 --> 00:02:27.984
Both horns exploded into shrapnel.

37
00:02:32.536 --> 00:02:35.959
Zann and the others ducked, covering their heads until the dust settled.

38
00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.441
Then Venna stood up.

39
00:02:38.461 --> 00:02:41.224
"Now what are we going to do with Morb?"

40
00:02:41.464 --> 00:02:41.924
she asked.

41
00:02:41.944 --> 00:02:43.986
"There will have to be a trial."

42
00:02:44.006 --> 00:02:46.628
"Agreed," Zann's mother said.

43
00:02:46.648 --> 00:02:49.771
"Nax and I will have plenty of evidence to present."

44
00:02:50.512 --> 00:02:51.693
Zann's father nodded.

45
00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:55.696
"I imagine the Red Council will banish him to the Wastelands forever."

46
00:02:56.997 --> 00:02:57.838
Wyssa scowled.

47
00:02:58.138 --> 00:02:59.980
"I'll save you all the trouble."

48
00:03:00.808 --> 00:03:03.070
She yanked at Morb, who struggled weakly.

49
00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.931
"No!" he cried.

50
00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.412
"Don't let her take me!"

51
00:03:07.272 --> 00:03:11.815
Zann winced, remembering what Wyssa had said about feeding Morb to a scatter beast.

52
00:03:12.536 --> 00:03:14.036
Then he looked at his parents.

53
00:03:14.797 --> 00:03:18.319
Because of Morb, Zann had almost lost them all over again.

54
00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.242
Still, did even Morb deserve the fate Wyssa had in mind for him?

55
00:03:23.262 --> 00:03:25.764
"Wait!" Gliss stepped forward.

56
00:03:26.268 --> 00:03:30.552
"After you're finished with him"—she glanced at Morb— "will you do something else?"

57
00:03:31.532 --> 00:03:32.773
"What is it, girl?"

58
00:03:33.054 --> 00:03:34.134
Wyssa sounded impatient.

59
00:03:34.755 --> 00:03:37.617
"We visited a world called Skellia," Gliss said.

60
00:03:37.637 --> 00:03:41.600
"The waters were rising, and the people were scared.

61
00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.222
Can you help them?"

62
00:03:44.343 --> 00:03:46.304
Wyssa raised an eyebrow in surprise.

63
00:03:46.324 --> 00:03:48.826
"I know Skellia," she said.

64
00:03:49.587 --> 00:03:50.508
Her voice softened.

65
00:03:50.528 --> 00:03:55.872
"And yes, if the Skellians are ready to leave, I can help."

66
00:03:56.684 --> 00:03:57.844
Darb stepped forward too.

67
00:03:57.864 --> 00:04:00.845
"Also, can you return this mibbit to Pax?"

68
00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:02.406
"Of course.

69
00:04:02.946 --> 00:04:05.226
The Paxians must be worried about him."

70
00:04:06.087 --> 00:04:10.008
Wyssa waited while Darb rubbed the creature's ears before handing it over.

71
00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:12.208
Then she glanced around.

72
00:04:12.228 --> 00:04:16.089
"Any other errands you need me to handle for you?"

73
00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.270
Her tone was sharp, but Zann caught a twinkle in her eye.

74
00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:26.508
"I think that's it," he said, "but He hesitated, staring at Morb.

75
00:04:26.528 --> 00:04:27.808
"What are you going to do with him?"

76
00:04:27.828 --> 00:04:30.509
"Only what he deserves."

77
00:04:31.149 --> 00:04:32.730
Wyssa gave a jerk on the shackles.

78
00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.551
"I'm sure the queen can help direct you all home.

79
00:04:37.111 --> 00:04:41.432
Good-bye." Dragging Morb, Wyssa stepped into the wormhole.

80
00:04:42.132 --> 00:04:54.696
The evil villain cried, "Are we there yet?"

81
00:04:55.036 --> 00:04:57.922
Zann joked as he and his parents walked toward their house.

82
00:04:58.743 --> 00:05:01.205
Zing was circling overhead, whistling joyfully.

83
00:05:01.225 --> 00:05:04.368
"You tell me, son," his father joked back.

84
00:05:04.388 --> 00:05:06.249
"I've never been here before."

85
00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:11.554
After Wyssa had departed with Morb, the Roodian queen sorted through the wormholes.

86
00:05:12.254 --> 00:05:17.539
First she located the one leading into Wormwood, which Venna used to return to First City.

87
00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:22.844
Then, after a long search, the queen found the one leading into Swamp Bottom.

88
00:05:24.096 --> 00:05:29.200
"I can't wait to see what Boz has done with the interior," Zann's father said when they stopped

89
00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.020
in front of their house.

90
00:05:30.861 --> 00:05:31.661
His wife chuckled.

91
00:05:31.681 --> 00:05:34.503
"Don't expect too much," she warned.

92
00:05:34.523 --> 00:05:37.745
"My father was never much of a decorator."

93
00:05:38.586 --> 00:05:39.507
They headed inside.

94
00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:41.668
There was no sign of Boz.

95
00:05:41.688 --> 00:05:44.530
"Look!" Zann's mother exclaimed.

96
00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:48.372
"Those are the blink images from our trip to the Flower Forest."

97
00:05:49.653 --> 00:05:52.215
She and Zann's father hurried over for a closer look.

98
00:05:52.976 --> 00:05:54.877
Meanwhile Zann heard footsteps.

99
00:05:55.577 --> 00:05:58.158
A moment later his grandfather burst into the room.

100
00:05:58.179 --> 00:06:00.700
"Zann!" Boz exclaimed.

101
00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:03.021
He rushed over and hugged Zann tightly.

102
00:06:03.742 --> 00:06:06.903
Then he gently shoved him away and glared.

103
00:06:06.923 --> 00:06:10.185
"Where in all the worlds have you been?

104
00:06:10.925 --> 00:06:12.186
I've been worried sick!

105
00:06:12.946 --> 00:06:20.370
The Directory showed nothing of your whereabouts, and every spell I tried was—" Zann's mother stepped up behind

106
00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.952
Boz. "Hello, Dad," she said.

107
00:06:23.352 --> 00:06:24.513
"Did you miss me too?"

108
00:06:25.374 --> 00:06:26.835
Boz's jaw dropped.

109
00:06:27.175 --> 00:06:28.536
"Asta?" he whispered.

110
00:06:29.097 --> 00:06:34.301
Then, his nose quivering wildly and his eyes widening, he spun around.

111
00:06:34.321 --> 00:06:36.403
"And Nax too!

112
00:06:37.404 --> 00:06:40.926
What—how did you Zann laughed.

113
00:06:40.946 --> 00:06:43.068
"We'll tell you all about it!"

114
00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:47.332
That night Zann fell asleep happy.

115
00:06:48.232 --> 00:06:52.276
At one point, in the middle of the night, he was awakened by a terrible dream.

116
00:06:53.136 --> 00:06:54.117
Morb had escaped!

117
00:06:54.457 --> 00:06:59.359
And Zann's parents were in trouble But as Zann looked around, he remembered where he was.

118
00:07:00.179 --> 00:07:01.520
He was back in his own bed.

119
00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.580
His parents and Boz were nearby.

120
00:07:04.441 --> 00:07:06.662
Zing's fiery breath was warming his toes.

121
00:07:07.382 --> 00:07:11.784
For the first time in four years, Zann felt content.
